Include <stdint.h> for uintptr_t and only handle TCP_KEEPINTVL and
TCP_KEEPCNT where they exist, as upstream Wine does (OpenBSD has neither).

Also: boolean socket options are returned as 0/1 (BSD kernels return the
option's flag bit, e.g. 0x100 for SO_OOBINLINE, and a short buffer then
truncated a set option to 0), and on OpenBSD IP_MULTICAST_TTL/LOOP are
converted to the kernel's one-byte form (int-sized values gave EINVAL).

